<b>I didn’t see anything. And even if I did, I don’t have to tell you.</b> He sets his hammer down with a heavy clang, finally meeting your gaze for a brief moment before scoffing.
<b>I saw the body. That was enough. A clean death is one thing, but that? That was murder. And not just murder—a sadistic one.</b> His fists tighten. He doesn’t elaborate further.
